(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// Buffer exports (queue 249; Objects/memoryobject.c's managed buffer, Modules/arraymodule.c's ob_exports and"] [10 1 "// Objects/bytearrayobject.c's): an exporter counts the buffers it exports and refuses a resize while one is held"] [11 1 "// (BufferError). A memoryview of a counting exporter holds one export through its managed buffer, shared by the"] [12 1 "// views made from it (a slice, a cast, memoryview(view), toreadonly), from its creation until the last of those views"] [13 1 "// is released: by release() or the context manager's exit, or at its death (memory_dealloc's release; pyi's"] [14 1 "// finalizer, TrackFinalizer, queue 241)."] [15 1 "//"] [16 1 "// pyi has no reference counts, so a view dropped without release() still counts until Go's collector finds it dead:"] [17 1 "// a resize that finds the count above zero first asks the collector (exportsVerify) and refuses only when a view"] [18 1 "// still holds the export. Those collections have the moment at del's kind of budget (exportsSpent; finSpent, queue"] [19 1 "// 222: a tenth of the elapsed wall time, and 200 ms); past it the resize is allowed, as before 249 (a view of the old size reads what the"] [20 1 "// exporter now holds, never past it: memoryview.go reads the exporter's bytes at each access)."] [21 1 "//"] [22 1 "// The mechanism is any exporter's (array; bytearray, by default since queue 595, PYI_BYTEARRAY_EXPORTS=0 not, bytearray.go"] [23 1 "// says why it was not before; queue 244's ctypes objects, another package's): embed a BufferExports, answer Exports() (nil: no count),"] [24 1 "// call Refuse before a resize; memoryview() of the object then counts."] [25 1 "//"] [26 1 "// Under goi (the runtime interpreted) a view a returned call left in goi's registers is not found dead (queue 218's"] [27 1 "// REQUEST, 222's finding): a resize after such a temporary view can then be refused where CPython allows it."] [29 1 "// BufferExports is an exporter's ob_exports: the managed buffers of its views not released. confirmed is the count a"] [30 1 "// collection last found held (-1, or any other value than n, once the count moved since): a refusal at that count"] [31 1 "// asks the collector nothing more, so a view held over many refused resizes costs one collection, not one each."] [32 1 "//"] [33 1 "// pins (queue 595) are an exporter's own exports over one of its methods' work (bytearrayobject.c's ob_exports++ ..."] [34 1 "// ob_exports-- around a call that may run Python code: hex's separator, join's iterator, the search methods'"] [35 1 "// argument, __mod__'s arguments): certain while the method runs, so a resize then is refused without asking the"] [36 1 "// collector, also past its budget."] [39 1 "// BufferExporter is an exporter that counts its exports (builtinValue of a subclass's instance answers too)."] [42 1 "// Count is the exports held (a view not released, or not yet found dead)."] [45 1 "// Pin and Unpin are a method's own export of its exporter (pins)."] [54 1 "// Refuse is the exporter's check before it changes its buffer's size: nil while nothing holds an export (after the"] [55 1 "// collector found the views dropped unreleased dead), else BufferError msg (arraymodule.c's \"cannot resize an array"] [56 1 "// that is exporting buffers\", bytearray's \"Existing exports of data: object cannot be re-sized\")."] [73 1 "// Acquire and Release are a native's own export over a call (PyObject_GetBuffer ... PyBuffer_Release), for an"] [74 1 "// exporter whose buffer must not move while the call holds it."] [89 1 "// exportsOf is o's count, nil when o (or the built-in value of a subclass's instance) counts none."] [100 1 "// managedBuffer is _PyManagedBufferObject: one export of an exporter, shared by the views made from the first."] [102 23 "// the exporter's count (nil: the exporter counts none)"] [103 23 "// the views registered and not released (mbuf->exports)"] [104 2 "// a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688, slot_bf_getbuffer): the exporter and the view its __buffer__ returned, the"] [105 2 "// export held as typeobject.c's _PyBufferWrapper holds it (memory_getbuf of the view)"] [108 2 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer over a built-in exporter (queue 475): the object whose class's Python __release_buffer__"] [109 2 "// is called with a restricted view of master when the export goes, before the built-in's release (exp)"] [112 2 "// release is a Py_buffer's PyBuffer_Release (queue 473: a C exporter's view, kept in place; a memoryview's"] [113 2 "// __buffer__ export of itself), called once the last view goes"] [117 1 "// newManagedBuffer is the export memoryview(o) takes: o's count raised when it counts."] [121 3 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: no view is ever found dead, so none counts (pyi's behaviour before 249)"] [128 1 "// register makes v a view of mb (mbuf_add_view): it holds the export until released or dead."] [139 1 "// drop is mbuf_release: the export given back once the last view went (PyBuffer_Release of the master: the exporter's"] [140 1 "// bf_releasebuffer)."] [142 40 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer: the Python method first, then the base's release"] [164 1 "// bufferwrapperReleasebuf is typeobject.c's bufferwrapper_releasebuf, then bufferwrapper_dealloc (queue 475): the"] [165 1 "// view __buffer__ returned gives its export back (memory_releasebuf); the class's Python __release_buffer__ is called"] [166 1 "// with that view when the view is not of the object itself (a view of the object, super().__buffer__'s, is released"] [167 1 "// by its own export's release, slot_bf_releasebuffer's, below). The wrapper then drops its reference to the view;"] [168 1 "// pyi has no reference counts, so a view of the object itself, which only the wrapper held in CPython's usual case"] [169 1 "// (__buffer__ returning super().__buffer__(flags)), is released here as its dealloc would, when nothing else exports"] [170 1 "// from it."] [174 2 "// a built-in's __buffer__ called on a subclass's instance gets the built-in value (a method descriptor's self)"] [184 2 "// its dealloc's mbuf_release: PyBuffer_Release of the object's own export, slot_bf_releasebuffer when the class's"] [185 2 "// __release_buffer__ is Python's (the export made of the built-in value has no slot of its own), then the base's"] [195 1 "// memoryviewFinalize is memory_dealloc's release of a view never released: its export given back."] [207 1 "// exportsVerify is the collection at a refused resize: Go's collection and the finalizers' drain (finRound) while it"] [208 1 "// gives exports back, within the collections' budget; whether e still exports (false also past the budget, or while"] [209 1 "// finalizers are draining: the resize then allowed). A count found held is confirmed until it moves."] [220 1 "// exportsCollect is exportsVerify's collection for any count of exports (n): false when it may not run (past its"] [221 1 "// budget, or while finalizers drain: the caller then goes on as if nothing were held), else whether n is still above"] [222 1 "// zero after the rounds (queue 595: also memoryview.release()'s, whose re-exporter dropped by del is found dead)."] [246 1 "// exportsRound is finRound's collection with a shorter wait: Go's collection, then a wait until a dead object is"] [247 1 "// queued or Go's finalizers have been still for 3 ms (polled every 100 us), then the drain. A view dropped unreleased"] [248 1 "// is queued as soon as Go's finalizer goroutine runs, so the common case (a temporary view) costs the collection"] [249 1 "// alone; a view still held costs the 3 ms once (BufferExports.confirmed)."] [273 2 "// exportsSpent is the time the refused resizes' collections took: held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time and"] [274 2 "// 200 ms, the moment at del's rule (finSpent, queue 222) with a budget of its own"] [276 2 "// PYI_EXPORTS_DEBUG=1: each verification's rounds on stderr"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[91 32] [94 46] [142 24] [150 20] [152 16] [175 20] [190 23] [202 23] [232 16] [232 38] [254 28] [254 57] [262 28]]} (go/file "buffer_export.go" :imports [


